A||||0||Tryxalon||Sharing the Steering Column blues||||1||
Z||000000||Tryxalon||04-08-2001||10:59 PM||||Just as part of "shared memory" ... My 85 SE wouldn't start again.  Troubleshooting indicated that the problem was in the ignition switch.  <P>The car would start by shorting the starter and run if put into "run position" but wouldn't turn off, and feeling nothing turning the key ... and feeling no "clicks", detents or resistance in that operation. Couldn't turn it off ... and finally did - oF course it didn't start again. <P>After getting it towed home and going through the entire starting system again, I find that it has to be something IN the steering column. I took the column apart (Oliver's Site has some great instructions on this)  <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/fieroidx.html</A>  <P>And I found out the "Ignition Rack" was broken - a pot metal connection activated by the key and moving the the rod that actually works the ignition switch. At least it fell out in two pieces as I was disassembling the Column. <P>While taking out the pivot bushings ... I managed to break the housing they sit in (also pot metal). Oliver's must have been less "set in" - or I used too much "BF&I". Those Tilt Wheel Pivot Bushing were really in there.  Even with PB blaster ... I still wound up cracking the socket they go into - and they are still fully seated!! <P>I share all of this because as I get time, I'm going to go find a replacement steering column from a junkyard ... Looks like it would be easier to replace it with a new one and just transfer my lock than to continue with this. Maybe a non-tilt version.<P>Not really "bitching" ... just sharing "lessons learned". <P>||||reg||1
